  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d4ecd1a615a340f4c9104ca01624d106, type: 3}
  m_Name: Gamble
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::YourCall.Dilemma
  _id: gamble
  _verb: 2
  _weight: 2
  _narratorPrompt: A whole crowd this time, every one of them waiting on your mark.
    Spare them yourself, clean and certain, and never learn what they were worth.
    Or trust the crowd to hold the line, and let them live only if enough of them
    would have held it for a stranger. You spent a career deciding what people deserved.
    Tonight it rides on what they deserve from each other. Your call.
  _choices:
  - _id: hold
    _label: hold the line
    _narratorReact: You held the line yourself and spared every one of them. You
      would not trust them to hold it without you. Watch the count come in, and wonder
      what that says about you, not them.
    _narratorReactStruck: 
    _struckParty: 
    _gambledParty: 
    _route: 
    _diverts: 0
    _seedVotes: 0
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 3
      _value: -1
  - _id: roll
    _label: roll the dice
    _narratorReact: You trusted the crowd, and this time enough of them held. You
      gambled strangers' lives on strangers, and it paid. Sleep well on that if you
      can.
    _narratorReactStruck: You trusted the crowd to hold the line, and not enough
      of them did. You bet their lives on each other, and the count came up short.
      They will never know it was you who dealt the hand.
    _struckParty: 
    _gambledParty: crowd
    _route: 
    _diverts: 0
    _seedVotes: 0
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 3
      _value: 1
    - _axis: 0
      _value: 1
  _statsHeading: how the crowd leaned
  _crowdSafeFraction: 0.43
  _crowdThreshold: 0.5
  _thresholdLabel: needed
